.TH SITUC 1 "" "situ" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
situc \- compiler for situ byte-layout schemas
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B situc
.RI [ --diagnostics
.IR text | json ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.I schema
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B situ
is a schema language for data whose layout is decided by somebody else:
network protocols, file formats and device registers, where the bytes are
fixed and the reader has to match them exactly. A schema states what the
bytes are, and
.B situc
derives everything else from it.
.PP
What it derives is not only accessors. A schema also produces a capability
map saying what each field costs to reach, a byte-level wire contract that
makes an incompatible edit visible in review, a Wireshark dissector, a fuzz
harness, and a test suite holding the generated code to the map.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B build
Generate accessors.
.B \-\-target
selects
.IR c ", " cpp ", " rust " or " python ;
.B \-\-out
names the output directory.
.TP
.B map
Emit the capability map, or with
.B \-\-check
compare against the committed one.
.TP
.B wire
Emit the byte-level contract, or with
.B \-\-check
classify what an edit changed.
.TP
.B doc
RFC-style byte-layout diagrams and a field reference.
.TP
.B explain
One path's capability vector and the blame chain behind it.
.TP
.B advise
Ranked, costed suggestions for a schema.
.TP
.B diff
Capability changes between two revisions of a schema.
.TP
.B gen-checks
Tests holding the generated accessors to the capability map.
.TP
.B gen-fuzz
A fuzz harness per parseable struct.
.TP
.B gen-dissector
A Wireshark dissector in Lua.
.TP
.B gen-tests
Golden-vector tests from a
.I .vectors
file.
.TP
.B gen-codec-tests
Property tests from codec signatures.
.TP
.B gen-derived
Implementations from kernel descriptions.
.TP
.B import-proto
Import a
.I .proto
as a description of its wire format.
.TP
.B dump-ast
Print the parsed AST, as a tree or back as situ source.
.TP
.B lsp
Run a language server over stdio.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-diagnostics \fItext\fR|\fIjson\fR
Diagnostic output format.
.I json
is for editors and CI.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B situc
exits 0 when it accepted the schema and did what was asked, and non-zero
when it refused. A refusal is a diagnostic with a blame chain, not a stack
trace.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/situc/std
Standard schemas, including the codec signatures.
.SH SEE ALSO
The generated C requires the header and static library in
.BR libsitu-dev .
